% Lesson 8 — runnable answer (exercise 2): a well-connected diamond
% where DRed's over-delete is much larger than the true damage.
% Deleting edge(s, m1) implicates every path through m1 — but every one
% of them survives via m2 and is re-derived.
%   python3 incremental.py exercises/08-answers.dl -u 'edge(s, m1)~.'

edge(s, m1).   edge(s, m2).
edge(m1, t).   edge(m2, t).
edge(t, u1).   edge(u1, u2).  edge(u2, u3).

path(X, Y) :- edge(X, Y).
path(X, Z) :- edge(X, Y), path(Y, Z).
